==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|la|i}}, [[minuscule]] of {{m|la|I}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|en|/ə/|/aɪ/|/ɪ/|/i/|/iː/}}
* {{sense|letter name}} {{enPR|ī}}, {{IPA|en|/aɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-i.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|aye|eye}}

====Letter====
{{letter|en}}

# {{Latn-def|en|letter|9|i}}

=====Usage notes=====
The English letter {{m|en|i}} represents many different sounds, often the diphthong {{IPAchar|/aɪ/}} (from Middle English {{IPAchar|/iː/}}), as in the pronoun {{m|en|I}}, or {{IPAchar|/ɪ/}} as in {{m|en|bit|b'''i'''t}}. In borrowings, it may represent {{IPAchar|/iː/}} as well.

